Practical 6: Scrum Board & Sprint Management
We’ll complete this practical in your existing Syllogix (SYL) Jira project. Follow each step in order.

A. Create and configure a Scrum Board
Step 1 — Create the board
1. Open Jira and go to Boards (or View all boards).
2. Click Create board.
3. Select Create a Scrum board.
4. Choose Board from an existing project.
5. Enter the board name: SYL Scrum Board.
6. Select your Syllogix project.
7. Click Create board.

Step 2 — Configure the board
1. Open the new Scrum board.
2. Go to Board settings.
3. Open Columns.
4. Check that the columns match your workflow:
- To Do
- In Progress
- Done
If your project has an In Review status, map it to an appropriate column too.

B. Create and start a Sprint
1. Open your Scrum board and select Backlog.
2. Click Create sprint.
3. Rename it Student Management Sprint 1.
4. Add your existing student-management issues from the backlog. For example:
   - SYL-2 — Create Student Registration Page
   - Design Student Database — if you created it
   - Your student-management Bug — if you created it
5. Click Start sprint.
6. Set the duration to 2 weeks.
7. Enter the sprint goal: Complete the initial student registration and database work.
8. Click Start to confirm.

C. Complete the Sprint and generate the Sprint Report
Step 1 — Complete the sprint
1. Open Active sprints.
2. Move the issues you completed to Done.
3. Click Complete sprint.
4. If Jira asks about unfinished issues, move them to the backlog or another sprint.
5. Confirm completion.

Step 2 — Generate the Sprint Report
1. Open your Scrum board.
2. Select Reports.
3. Choose Sprint Report.
4. Select Student Management Sprint 1.
5. Review the completed and incomplete issues shown in the report.
